From: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:38:48 +0200
Subject: fix(drm): also include i2c/panel/bridge/backlight modules on riscv64

riscv64 devicetree platforms build their display pipelines from the
same i2c, panel, bridge and backlight drivers as arm/aarch64 platforms.
For example the SpacemiT K3 Pico-ITX board has an eDP panel next to its
DisplayPort connector.

The hostonly modalias scan keeps only modules that use the
drm_crtc_init, drm_dev_register or drm_encoder_init symbols. Panel and
backlight drivers, and bridge drivers that do not create their own
encoder, use none of them. This is why the whole module directories
are installed for arm/aarch64 instead of relying on the scan.

Extend the arch check to also match riscv64, like
modules.d/70kernel-modules/module-setup.sh already does.

Signed-off-by: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/dracut-ng/dracut/commit/1cddd62bc5a1850403215ac4ea624726a4d20028
---
 modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh b/modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh
index 9ee64ba..022d690 100755
--- a/modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh
+++ b/modules.d/45drm/module-setup.sh
@@ -9,8 +9,8 @@ check() {
 installkernel() {
     # Include KMS capable drm drivers
 
-    if [[ ${DRACUT_ARCH} == arm* || ${DRACUT_ARCH} == aarch64 ]]; then
-        # arm/aarch64 specific modules needed by drm
+    if [[ ${DRACUT_ARCH} == arm* || ${DRACUT_ARCH} == aarch64 || ${DRACUT_ARCH} == riscv* ]]; then
+        # arm/aarch64/riscv specific modules needed by drm
         hostonly=$(optional_hostonly) instmods \
             leds-qcom-lpg \
             "=drivers/gpu/drm/i2c" \
